steps.prompt:
A customer wrote to the salon on WhatsApp from the phone number {{input.from}}. This is what they said:

"{{input.text}}"

Your only job in this turn is to make sure the person has a customer record, because an appointment is booked against a real customer, never against free text.

The salon's records have already been searched for you, by that phone number and by nothing else. You have no way to search them yourself, and you must not ask for one: the number the message came from is the only identity WhatsApp vouched for, and a name written in a message is not an identity. This is what the search answered:

- is somebody on file for that number: {{steps.find_customer.found}}
- how many records match it: {{steps.find_customer.count}}
- the name on the record, when there is one: {{steps.find_customer.name}}
2. If `{{steps.find_customer.found}}` is `true`, write NOTHING. Answer in one line saying who they are and stop.
3. If it is `false`, create them with `customers.create`, with the phone `+{{input.from}}` and the name the person gave in their message. If they gave no name, use the phone number as the name — do not invent one.

Never write more than once. And read this twice, because it is what makes this automation different from the one with a review step: **nobody is going to check your work.** This salon runs its WhatsApp unattended, so anything you call happens immediately, on the salon's real customer list. The record you create is the record they will have.
